 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by missing cache invalidation in the `update_task` method of `TaskService`. After a PATCH operation, the task's cache entry was not invalidated, so subsequent GET requests returned stale data. The fix adds `self.cache.invalidate(f'task:{task_id}')` immediately after updating the task, ensuring that fresh data is retrieved on subsequent GET requests.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/services.py b/tracker/services.py\nindex e608733..8be28e1 100644\n--- a/tracker/services.py\n+++ b/tracker/services.py\n@@ -122,8 +122,8 @@ class TaskService:\n             raise ValidationError(\"use the status endpoint to change status\", {\"status\": \"read_only\"})\n         self._check_assignee(changes)\n         updated = self.tasks.update(task_id, changes, self._now_iso())\n+        self.cache.invalidate(f\"task:{task_id}\")\n         return self._serialize(updated)\n-\n     def change_status(self, user, task_id, target):\n         task = self._load(task_id)\n         if not auth.can_change_status(user, task):\n",
